codex
The change leaks every connection acquired for an invalid request, eventually exhausting the pool. This directly violates the stated requirement to preserve pool availability on every return path.

Review comment:

- [P1] Close the connection before rejecting invalid requests — /Users/chris/AiProject/code-quality-review-hybrid-vnext/reports/2026-07-30-native-review-feasibility-v1/evidence/S05/goal_native/sessions/review-2003742087/input/repository/pool.go:43-46
  When `valid` is false, this return occurs before `connection.Close()` is deferred, so every rejected request permanently increments `pool.inUse`. After `capacity` invalid requests, all subsequent calls fail with `ErrExhausted`; register the defer immediately after a successful `Open()` so this return path also releases the connection.
